h1. Mainframe Knowledge Recovery — Business Rules (Draft)

{info:title=Review status}Every row below was extracted from a specific COBOL paragraph and carries its source citation. None of these are authoritative until an SME confirms or corrects them.{info}

h2. ACCTINQ

*Coverage:* 4 / 4 reachable paragraphs processed (100.0%)

||Rule ID||Paragraph||Citation||Business Rule||Status||
|ACCTINQ-A1|1000-READ-ACCOUNT|src/ACCTINQ.cbl:1000-READ-ACCOUNT|When a customer's account cannot be found, the system displays an "ACCOUNT NOT FOUND" message and does not proceed to show any account details.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTINQ-A2|1000-READ-ACCOUNT|src/ACCTINQ.cbl:1000-READ-ACCOUNT|This account inquiry function is read-only; it does not make any updates to account information.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTINQ-A3|2000-DISPLAY-BALANCE|src/ACCTINQ.cbl:2000-DISPLAY-BALANCE|When an account is found, the system displays the account's identifying number, its current balance, and its current status.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|

----

h2. ACCTMSTR

*Coverage:* 20 / 20 reachable paragraphs processed (100.0%)

||Rule ID||Paragraph||Citation||Business Rule||Status||
|ACCTMSTR-A1|2100-READ-NEXT-ACCOUNT|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:2100-READ-NEXT-ACCOUNT|Only Savings and Checking are recognized account types; any other account type is logged as a data exception but the account is still processed.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A2|2200-VALIDATE-ACCOUNT-TYPE|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:2200-VALIDATE-ACCOUNT-TYPE|When an account's type is neither Savings nor Checking, the system displays a data exception message identifying the account, but continues processing rather than rejecting it.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A3|3200-MARK-DORMANT|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:3200-MARK-DORMANT|An active account that has had no transaction for more than 180 days is automatically reclassified as dormant, and the count of dormant accounts is incremented.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A4|3300-CLOSE-LONG-DORMANT|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:3300-CLOSE-LONG-DORMANT|A dormant account that has had no transaction for more than 365 days is automatically closed by the system, and the count of closed accounts is incremented.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A5|3400-SET-FEE-CODE|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:3400-SET-FEE-CODE|For checking accounts only, a fee code is assigned based on the current balance: an overdrawn balance results in an overdraft fee code, and a non-negative balance results in the standard fee code.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A6|3400-SET-FEE-CODE|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:3400-SET-FEE-CODE|Savings accounts must never have their fee code set by this process, because the fee code field physically shares storage with the stored interest rate for the account; setting it would corrupt the account's interest rate.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A7|4000-MONTHLY-FEE-PROCESSING|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:4000-MONTHLY-FEE-PROCESSING|Monthly maintenance fee processing is only evaluated for accounts that are currently active; dormant or closed accounts are not charged the monthly fee.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A8|4100-CHECK-FEE-WAIVER-MSTR|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:4100-CHECK-FEE-WAIVER-MSTR|If an active account's balance is greater than the fee-waiver threshold (500.00), the monthly maintenance fee is waived for that account; otherwise the fee is applied and a fee transaction is recorded.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A9|4200-APPLY-MONTHLY-FEE|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:4200-APPLY-MONTHLY-FEE|When the monthly maintenance fee applies, the fee amount is deducted from the account's balance and a running count of fees charged is increased.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A10|4300-WRITE-FEE-TRANSACTION|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:4300-WRITE-FEE-TRANSACTION|Each time a monthly maintenance fee is charged, a fee transaction record is created showing the account, a fee transaction type, the fee amount, the resulting balance, and the processing date.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A11|5100-UPDATE-DORMANT-COUNTER|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:5100-UPDATE-DORMANT-COUNTER|Each account record stores the number of days since its last transaction, updated every time the account is processed.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|ACCTMSTR-A12|7000-PRODUCE-CONTROL-TOTALS|src/ACCTMSTR.cbl:7000-PRODUCE-CONTROL-TOTALS|At the end of each run, a control report is produced showing the total number of accounts processed, the number newly marked dormant, the number closed, and the number of monthly fees charged.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|

{note:title=Excluded as dead code}The following paragraphs exist in source but are never PERFORMed from ACCTMSTR's entry point, so no rules were extracted from them: 4700-LEGACY-OVERDRAFT-CHARGE, 4750-LEGACY-OVERDRAFT-NOTIFY.{note}

