h2. DEPOSIT

*Coverage:* 8 / 8 reachable paragraphs processed (100.0%)

||Rule ID||Paragraph||Citation||Business Rule||Status||
|DEPOSIT-A1|2000-READ-ACCOUNT|src/DEPOSIT.cbl:2000-READ-ACCOUNT|If the account number on the deposit cannot be found in the account file, the deposit is rejected.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|DEPOSIT-A2|2100-VALIDATE-ACCOUNT|src/DEPOSIT.cbl:2100-VALIDATE-ACCOUNT|A deposit is rejected if the account status is closed.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|DEPOSIT-A3|2100-VALIDATE-ACCOUNT|src/DEPOSIT.cbl:2100-VALIDATE-ACCOUNT|If the account is currently dormant, a deposit reactivates the account by changing its status to active.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|DEPOSIT-A4|3000-POST-DEPOSIT|src/DEPOSIT.cbl:3000-POST-DEPOSIT|The deposit amount is added to the account's current balance.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|DEPOSIT-A5|3000-POST-DEPOSIT|src/DEPOSIT.cbl:3000-POST-DEPOSIT|When a deposit is posted, the account's last-transaction date is updated to today's date.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|DEPOSIT-A6|3100-CHECK-FEE-WAIVER|src/DEPOSIT.cbl:3100-CHECK-FEE-WAIVER|If the account balance after the deposit is at or above the fee waiver threshold, the monthly maintenance fee is waived for this account.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|DEPOSIT-A7|3100-CHECK-FEE-WAIVER|src/DEPOSIT.cbl:3100-CHECK-FEE-WAIVER|If the account balance after the deposit is below the fee waiver threshold, a monthly maintenance fee is immediately deducted from the account balance.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|DEPOSIT-A8|4000-WRITE-TRANSACTION|src/DEPOSIT.cbl:4000-WRITE-TRANSACTION|Every accepted deposit is recorded as a transaction log entry showing the account, a deposit transaction type code, the deposit amount, the resulting account balance, and the transaction date.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|DEPOSIT-A9|4000-WRITE-TRANSACTION|src/DEPOSIT.cbl:4000-WRITE-TRANSACTION|The account record is updated on file to reflect the new balance and status resulting from the deposit.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|

----

h2. INTCALC

*Coverage:* 9 / 9 reachable paragraphs processed (100.0%)

||Rule ID||Paragraph||Citation||Business Rule||Status||
|INTCALC-A1|2100-CHECK-ELIGIBLE|src/INTCALC.cbl:2100-CHECK-ELIGIBLE|Monthly interest is calculated only for accounts that are both a savings account and currently in active status. Checking accounts, dormant accounts, and closed accounts never earn interest.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|INTCALC-A2|2200-APPLY-RATE-TIER|src/INTCALC.cbl:2200-APPLY-RATE-TIER|If an eligible account's balance is $10,000.00 or more, the account earns a bonus annual interest rate of 4.5%, overriding the rate normally on file for that account.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|INTCALC-A3|2200-APPLY-RATE-TIER|src/INTCALC.cbl:2200-APPLY-RATE-TIER|If an eligible account's balance is below $10,000.00, the account earns the annual interest rate stored on the account record rather than the bonus rate.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|INTCALC-A4|2200-APPLY-RATE-TIER|src/INTCALC.cbl:2200-APPLY-RATE-TIER|The stored interest rate on an account record is only meaningful for savings accounts; the same storage location is used for a fee code on other account types, so this rate value must only be used after confirming the account is a savings account.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|INTCALC-A5|2300-COMPUTE-INTEREST|src/INTCALC.cbl:2300-COMPUTE-INTEREST|Monthly interest for an eligible account is calculated as the account balance multiplied by the applicable annual interest rate, divided by 12, rounded to the nearest cent.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|INTCALC-A6|3000-POST-INTEREST|src/INTCALC.cbl:3000-POST-INTEREST|The calculated monthly interest is added to the account's balance at the time interest is posted.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|INTCALC-A7|3000-POST-INTEREST|src/INTCALC.cbl:3000-POST-INTEREST|When interest is posted, the account's last-transaction date is updated to the current processing date.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|INTCALC-A8|4000-WRITE-TRANSACTION|src/INTCALC.cbl:4000-WRITE-TRANSACTION|Each time interest is posted to an account, a transaction record is created with transaction type 'IN' (interest), recording the interest amount, the account's balance after posting, and the transaction date.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|INTCALC-A9|4000-WRITE-TRANSACTION|src/INTCALC.cbl:4000-WRITE-TRANSACTION|The account's master record is updated (rewritten) to reflect the new balance whenever interest is posted.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|

----

h2. STMTGEN

*Coverage:* 7 / 7 reachable paragraphs processed (100.0%)

||Rule ID||Paragraph||Citation||Business Rule||Status||
|STMTGEN-A1|3000-PRINT-HEADER|src/STMTGEN.cbl:3000-PRINT-HEADER|Each customer statement begins with a header line showing the account identifier and the current account balance.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|STMTGEN-A2|4000-PRINT-TRANSACTIONS|src/STMTGEN.cbl:4000-PRINT-TRANSACTIONS|For each account being statemented, only transactions belonging to that same account are listed on its statement.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|STMTGEN-A3|4000-PRINT-TRANSACTIONS|src/STMTGEN.cbl:4000-PRINT-TRANSACTIONS|Each transaction line printed on the statement shows the transaction type, amount, and date.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|STMTGEN-A4|5000-UPDATE-LAST-STMT-DATE|src/STMTGEN.cbl:5000-UPDATE-LAST-STMT-DATE|Whenever a statement is generated for an account, the account's last-activity date is reset to the current date, even if the account had no actual customer transactions during the statement period. This prevents the account from later being flagged as dormant solely due to the lack of transactions in that cycle.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|

