h2. WITHDRWL

*Coverage:* 8 / 8 reachable paragraphs processed (100.0%)

||Rule ID||Paragraph||Citation||Business Rule||Status||
|WITHDRWL-A1|2000-READ-ACCOUNT|src/WITHDRWL.cbl:2000-READ-ACCOUNT|If the account number on the withdrawal request cannot be found on file, the withdrawal is rejected.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|WITHDRWL-A2|2100-VALIDATE-STATUS|src/WITHDRWL.cbl:2100-VALIDATE-STATUS|A withdrawal is rejected if the account is closed or dormant; the customer must reactivate a dormant account with a deposit before they can withdraw funds.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|WITHDRWL-A3|2200-VALIDATE-FUNDS|src/WITHDRWL.cbl:2200-VALIDATE-FUNDS|A withdrawal is rejected if it would reduce the account balance below a required $100.00 overdraft cushion.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|WITHDRWL-A4|3000-POST-WITHDRAWAL|src/WITHDRWL.cbl:3000-POST-WITHDRAWAL|When a withdrawal is approved, the withdrawal amount is subtracted from the account balance and the account's last transaction date is updated to today's date.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|
|WITHDRWL-A5|4000-WRITE-TRANSACTION|src/WITHDRWL.cbl:4000-WRITE-TRANSACTION|For every approved withdrawal, a transaction record is created recording the account number, a 'WD' (withdrawal) transaction type, the withdrawal amount, the resulting account balance, and today's date; the account's master record is then updated to reflect the new balance.|{status:colour=Yellow|title=NEEDS SME CONFIRM}|

